  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Rohit Dipak Patale vs State Of Maharashtra on 19 April, 2024 Author: Amit Borkar Bench: Amit Borkar 2024:Bhc-As:18345 2- Shabnoor In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No.1508 Of 2023 Shabnoor Ayub Rohit Dipak Patale ... Applicant Pathan Digitally signed by V/s. Shabnoor Ayub Pathan Date: 2024.04.20 15:25:55 +0530 The State of Maharashtra ... Respondent Mr. Rajesh More, for the Applicant. Mr. Pankaj P. Deokar, App for the State-Respondent. Coram : Amit Borkar, J.",
    "facts": "4. Apprehending arrest, the applicant filed an application under Section 438 of the Criminal Procedure Code, 1973 before the learned Sessions Judge, Sangli which was rejected by order dated 12 May 2023. Aggrieved thereby, the applicant has filed present anticipatory bail application. The materials surfaced during investigation against the applicant, do not connect the applicant with the truck driver or any other accused. In relation to the other three accused, the material in the form of call recording was available with the investigating agency.",
    "arguments": "Learned Advocate for the applicant submitted that though this Court refused to grant protection under Section 438 of the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973 in relation to other three persons. He, therefore submitted that interim relief granted by this Court deserves to be continued as the applicant has not breached the conditions imposed by this Court. 6. Learned APP submitted that since other three accused have been denied protection, the applicant could not have sought protection under Section 438 of the Cr.P.C. He submits that investigation is completed and charge-sheet has been filed.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned Advocate for the applicant submitted that though this Court refused to grant protection under Section 438 of the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973 in relation to other three persons. He, therefore submitted that interim relief granted by this Court deserves to be continued as the applicant has not breached the conditions imposed by this Court. 6. Learned APP submitted that since other three accused have been denied protection, the applicant could not have sought protection under Section 438 of the Cr.P.C. He submits that investigation is completed and charge-sheet has been filed.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
